{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Story hero (Our Story page)

  The Our Story page's opening block: full-bleed photo, left-weighted scrim,
  two-tone headline and the primary gold CTA, with the shared trust row over its
  lower edge.

  It replaces the flat sh-page-header band on this template only — sh-page-header
  is still what The Ritual and Contact open with, and is untouched.

  The headline is split into a plain part and an emphasised part per line rather
  than accepting HTML, so the gold words stay merchant-editable in the theme
  editor without opening a rich-text hole. `<em>` is restyled to normal weight
  and gold in shudhi-home.css — it is used for the semantics (emphasis), not the
  italics.

  Trust badges come from snippets/sh-trust-row.liquid, the same component the
  homepage hero renders, so the frosted-glass treatment is defined in exactly
  one place.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'shudhi-story.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}
{%- assign scrim = s.scrim | divided_by: 100.0 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  data-sh-reveal is what assets/sh-story-motion.js arms, and it replaces the
  [data-reveal] this band used to put on .sh-story-hero__copy. That attribute
  carried `opacity: 0` from shudhi-home.css §4, which meant an exception, a 404
  or a blocked script left this page's LCP band with an invisible headline, body
  and CTA. Every pre-state now lives behind .is-armed, which only ever appears
  next to the observer that clears it. See shudhi-story.css §28.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="sh sh-story-hero"
         {%- if s.animate %} data-sh-reveal{% endif -%}
         {%- if s.animate and s.cursor %} data-sh-cursor{% endif %}
         style="--sh-green-900:{{ s.bg }};--sh-story-hero-scrim:{{ scrim }};--sh-story-hero-h:{{ s.min_height }}px;">

  {%- comment -%} data-parallax is the SCROLL parallax from shudhi-home.js and it stays
      on the image. Pointer depth deliberately does NOT go here as well: two
      systems writing `transform` to one element fight every frame, and the house
      rule is one transform job per element. The pointer layers on this band are
      the copy column and the seal — the 2px and 3px of the design's depth stack —
      and the background keeps the 15px scroll travel it already had.

      Dimensions are the file's REAL ones. The fallback previously declared
      2000x1000 for an asset that was 1536x1024, so the browser reserved a box of
      the wrong shape for the LCP element. hero_frame_0240.webp is 1280x720.
      sizes="100vw" is stated because the image is full-bleed; without it the
      browser assumes 100vw anyway for the src, but the merchant branch's srcset
      needs it to pick correctly. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.image != blank -%}
    <img class="sh-story-hero__bg"{% if s.animate %} data-parallax{% endif %}
         src="{{ s.image | image_url: width: 2000 }}"
         srcset="{{ s.image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w,
                 {{ s.image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w,
                 {{ s.image | image_url: width: 2000 }} 2000w,
                 {{ s.image | image_url: width: 2600 }} 2600w"
         sizes="100vw"
         alt="{{ s.image.alt | default: s.title_l1 | escape }}"
         width="{{ s.image.width }}" height="{{ s.image.height }}"
         fetchpriority="high">
  {%- else -%}
    <img class="sh-story-hero__bg"{% if s.animate %} data-parallax{% endif %}
         src="{{ 'hero_frame_0240.webp' | asset_url }}"
         sizes="100vw"
         alt="" width="1280" height="720"
         fetchpriority="high">
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="sh-story-hero__scrim"></div>

  {%- comment -%} The resolve. A flat wash of the band's own background colour that
      starts opaque and clears over 1.1s, so the photograph appears to surface
      rather than snap in. Painted in --sh-green-900, so while the image is still
      in flight it is invisible against the section's own background and costs
      nothing; it only reads once there is a photo under it.

      Inert without .is-armed — no JS, no veil, and the photo is simply there. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.animate -%}<div class="sh-story-hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>{%- endif -%}

  <div class="sh-wrap">
    <div class="sh-story-hero__copy" data-sh-depth="0.25">

      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="sh-story-hero__eyebrow sh-eyebrow" data-sh-fade style="--i:0">
          {{ s.eyebrow }}{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}<i></i>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Each line is its own mask rather than two lines split by a <br>:
          the reveal needs an overflow box to slide the words up out of. .sh-w /
          .sh-w-in is the SHARED mask from §28 — the same pair band 6 uses on its
          heading words — so the page carries one mask geometry rather than the two
          it used to. The schema is untouched: title_l1/_em and title_l2/_em print
          the same text in the same order, and with `animate` off the wrappers are
          inert markup. Line 2 stays conditional; one line is a complete headline. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} THE SPACE BETWEEN THE TWO LINE SPANS IS LITERAL AND MUST STAY.
          Without it the accessible name fuses to "Rooted in Tradition.Crafted for
          Today." — there is no whitespace for the accessibility tree to infer
          between two adjacent spans, and this markup previously had none. It costs
          nothing visually: the <h1> is display:flex, and a flex container discards
          whitespace-only text nodes between its items, so the two lines land exactly
          where they did. Verify with
          `document.querySelector('.sh-story-hero__title').textContent`. {%- endcomment -%}
      <h1 class="sh-story-hero__title sh-serif">
        <span class="sh-w" style="--i:1"><span class="sh-w-in">{{ s.title_l1 }}{% if s.title_l1_em != blank %} <em>{{ s.title_l1_em }}</em>{% endif %}</span></span>
        {% if s.title_l2 != blank or s.title_l2_em != blank %}
          <span class="sh-w" style="--i:2"><span class="sh-w-in">{{ s.title_l2 }}{% if s.title_l2_em != blank %} <em>{{ s.title_l2_em }}</em>{% endif %}</span></span>
        {% endif %}
      </h1>

      <div class="sh-story-hero__rule" data-sh-fade style="--i:3"><i></i>{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}</div>

      {%- if s.body != blank -%}<p class="sh-story-hero__text" data-sh-fade style="--i:4">{{ s.body }}</p>{%- endif -%}

      <div class="sh-story-hero__cta" data-sh-fade style="--i:5">
        {%- if s.cta_label != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%} Falls back to the first band on THIS page. The old fallback was
              #our-story, which is sh-our-story's id — that section lives on the homepage
              (templates/index.json) and is not on this template, so clearing cta_link in
              the editor produced a link to nothing. #our-beginning is the anchor_id the
              our_beginning instance carries in templates/page.our-story.json. {%- endcomment -%}
          <a href="{{ s.cta_link | default: '#our-beginning' }}" class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid">
            {{ s.cta_label }} {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Sibling of .sh-wrap, not a child of it: the seal is positioned
      against the section's own box so it can sit out over the photo's open right
      side, which the wrap's max-width would otherwise stop it short of. Hidden
      entirely when the number is blank — an empty ring is not a design.

      depth 0.40 is ~3.2px of pointer travel, the design's "badge 3px" layer. The
      seal is the one element on this band that takes BOTH a depth and a fade,
      which is safe because they land on different properties of an element that
      is already its own containing block. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.seal_number != blank -%}
    {% render 'sh-gen-seal',
       number: s.seal_number,
       text_top: s.seal_text_top,
       text_bottom: s.seal_text_bottom,
       uid: section.id,
       depth: '0.40',
       reveal: 6 %}
  {%- endif -%}

  {% render 'sh-trust-row', blocks: section.blocks, class: 'sh-story-hero__trust' %}
</section>

{%- comment -%} Deferred and conditional, the same shape sh-ritual-benefits.liquid:224
    and sh-signature-product.liquid:179 use. One shared module serves all seven
    bands of this page; the seven <script src> tags resolve to one fetch and one
    execution (the __shSM guard). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if s.animate -%}
  <script src="{{ 'sh-story-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Story Hero",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our Story" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Headline" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Each line is split in two: the plain part, then the part shown in gold." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_l1", "label": "Line 1", "default": "Rooted in" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_l1_em", "label": "Line 1 — gold words", "default": "Tradition." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_l2", "label": "Line 2", "default": "Crafted for" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_l2_em", "label": "Line 2 — gold words", "default": "Today." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body text", "default": "Inspired by 4 generations of herbal wisdom, Shudhi Herbals brings ancient Ayurvedic recipes into your modern self-care rituals." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Primary button", "default": "Know our story" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Primary button link" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Generations seal" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The ring rotates slowly and the number counts up once, the first time it scrolls into view. Leave the number blank to hide the seal." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_number", "label": "Number", "default": "4" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_text_top", "label": "Top arc", "default": "Generations",
      "info": "Reads with the number, not around it — \"4 · Generations · of herbal wisdom\"." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_text_bottom", "label": "Bottom arc", "default": "of herbal wisdom" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Media" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Background image",
      "info": "Fills the whole band. Defaults to \"hero_frame_0240.webp\" in Assets (1280×720). Upload a wider image if the default looks soft on a large or high-density screen." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "scrim", "label": "Dark overlay strength", "min": 40, "max": 100, "step": 5, "default": 80, "unit": "%",
      "info": "Keeps the copy legible over the photo. Raise it if you swap in a lighter image." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "min_height", "label": "Band height", "min": 420, "max": 820, "step": 20, "default": 620, "unit": "px" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true,
      "info": "Turns off the whole entrance, the photo's scroll drift and the pointer depth together. The band still renders in full." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "cursor", "label": "Pointer depth (desktop)", "default": true,
      "info": "Nudges the copy and the seal a few pixels as the pointer moves. Desktop pointers only — ignored on touch, on narrow screens, and for anyone who has asked for reduced motion." },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#1b2411" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "trust", "name": "Trust badge", "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "leaf", "options": [
        { "value": "leaf-line", "label": "Leaf (fine)" }, { "value": "heart-line", "label": "Heart (fine)" },
        { "value": "hand-line", "label": "Hand (fine)" }, { "value": "rabbit-line", "label": "Rabbit (fine)" },
        { "value": "flask-line", "label": "Flask (fine)" },
        { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "heart", "label": "Heart" },
        { "value": "hand", "label": "Hand" }, { "value": "rabbit", "label": "Rabbit" },
        { "value": "lotus", "label": "Lotus" }, { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" },
        { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" }, { "value": "plant", "label": "Plant" },
        { "value": "badge", "label": "Badge" }, { "value": "recycle", "label": "Recycle" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "100% Natural" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "subtitle", "label": "Subtitle", "default": "No harsh chemicals" }
    ] }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "presets": [ { "name": "SH · Story Hero", "blocks": [
    { "type": "trust", "settings": { "icon": "leaf",       "title": "100% Natural",      "subtitle": "No harsh chemicals" } },
    { "type": "trust", "settings": { "icon": "flask-line", "title": "Lab Tested",        "subtitle": "Every batch verified" } },
    { "type": "trust", "settings": { "icon": "hand",       "title": "Handmade in India", "subtitle": "Small batch crafted" } },
    { "type": "trust", "settings": { "icon": "rabbit",     "title": "Cruelty Free",      "subtitle": "Kind to you & nature" } }
  ] } ]
}
{% endschema %}
